## Commits
### e6c0f53
test(state): pin loop detection and hook observation of array methods

With the mutating array methods running through the Proxy, the existing
read-then-write loop check and the state hooks see what each method does.
Pin that with tests on both kinds of state: every one of the seven
methods raises the named infinite-loop error in a synchronous top-level
effect, sort and reverse on fewer than two elements raise nothing, a
child effect and a converging microtask effect keep their exemption, and
onWrite and onRead report push with the arguments a direct access gives,
leaving out the equal-value length write.


